## My answer to the prompt

Here is a complete HTML + CSS example that creates glowing text with an animated rainbow gradient border around it.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Glowing Rainbow Text</title>

  <style>
    @property --angle {
      syntax: "<angle>";
      initial-value: 0deg;
      inherits: false;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      background: #05060a;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    }

    .rainbow-glow {
      --angle: 0deg;
      --border-width: 4px;
      --radius: 22px;

      position: relative;
      isolation: isolate;
      padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      border: var(--border-width) solid transparent;
      border-radius: var(--radius);

      background:
        linear-gradient(#0b0c14, #0b0c14) padding-box,
        conic-gradient(
          from var(--angle),
          #ff004d,
          #ff9a00,
          #ffee00,
          #00ff87,
          #00cfff,
          #7a5cff,
          #ff00d4,
          #ff004d
        ) border-box;

      animation: rainbow-spin 6s linear infinite;
    }

    /* Outer blurred rainbow halo */
    .rainbow-glow::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: -14px;
      z-index: -2;
      border-radius: calc(var(--radius) + 14px);
      background: conic-gradient(
        from var(--angle),
        #ff004d,
        #ff9a00,
        #ffee00,
        #00ff87,
        #00cfff,
        #7a5cff,
        #ff00d4,
        #ff004d
      );
      filter: blur(28px);
      opacity: 0.55;
      animation: rainbow-spin 6s linear infinite;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    /* Keeps the blurred halo from washing out the inside */
    .rainbow-glow::after {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      z-index: -1;
      border-radius: calc(var(--radius) - var(--border-width));
      background: #0b0c14;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .glowing-text {
      margin: 0;
      color: #fff;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 4.5rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-align: center;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      text-shadow:
        0 0 6px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9),
        0 0 18px rgba(0, 207, 255, 0.8),
        0 0 36px rgba(122, 92, 255, 0.7),
        0 0 70px rgba(255, 0, 212, 0.5);

      animation: glow-pulse 2.5s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
    }

    @keyframes rainbow-spin {
      to {
        --angle: 360deg;
      }
    }

    @keyframes glow-pulse {
      to {
        text-shadow:
          0 0 10px rgba(255, 255, 255, 1),
          0 0 26px rgba(0, 207, 255, 0.9),
          0 0 52px rgba(122, 92, 255, 0.8),
          0 0 95px rgba(255, 0, 212, 0.6);
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .rainbow-glow,
      .rainbow-glow::before,
      .glowing-text {
        animation: none;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="rainbow-glow">
    <h1 class="glowing-text">Rainbow Glow</h1>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

