Because this example loads images from the internet, Android needs the internet permission.

In `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`, make sure this line is inside the `<manifest>` tag and usually before `<application>`:

```xml
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
```

Run the app:

```bash
flutter run
```

If you want to use local images instead of network images:

1. Add images to your project, for example:

```text
assets/images/photo1.jpg
assets/images/photo2.jpg
assets/images/photo3.jpg
assets/images/photo4.jpg
```

2. Update `pubspec.yaml`:

```yaml
flutter:
  assets:
    - assets/images/
```

3. Replace `Image.network(...)` with:

```dart
Image.asset(
  'assets/images/photo1.jpg',
  fit: BoxFit.cover,
)
```

