The error is not saying that lists are unsupported by Unity. It is a C# compiler error caused by the name `IList` resolving to the generic interface `System.Collections.Generic.IList<T>` instead of the non-generic interface `System.Collections.IList`.

In C#, there are two relevant interfaces:

```csharp
System.Collections.IList
System.Collections.Generic.IList<T>
```

`System.Collections.Generic.IList<T>` is a generic type. It must be closed with a type argument:

```csharp
IList<int>
IList<string>
