## My answer to the prompt

A robust way to do this in Unity 2023 is to make a **surface-walking Rigidbody controller**:

1. Raycast/shape-cast to find the nearby walkable surface.
2. Use the surface hit normal as the character’s temporary “up” direction.
3. Rotate the character so its local `Y` axis matches that normal.
4. Move the character only on the tangent plane of that surface.
5. Apply a custom “gravity” or stick force toward the surface so it stays attached.

This works for cubes, spheres, and custom models as long as the surfaces have colliders.

---

# 1. Scene setup

## Walkable objects

Create a layer called:

```text
Walkable
```

Assign your cube, sphere, or custom model to this layer.

Add colliders:

| Object | Collider |
|---|---|
| Cube | `BoxCollider` |
| Sphere | `SphereCollider` |
| Custom static model | `MeshCollider` |

For a static custom level mesh, the `MeshCollider` usually does **not** need to be convex.

Important: keep the player on a different layer, for example:

```text
Player
```

Do not put the player on the `Walkable` layer, or your raycasts may detect the player itself unless you filter carefully.

---

## Player setup

Create a player GameObject:

```text
Player
└── VisualModel
```

On the root `Player`, add:

- `Rigidbody`
- `CapsuleCollider`
- The script below

Recommended Rigidbody settings:

```text
Use Gravity: false
Interpolate: Interpolate
Collision Detection: Continuous Dynamic
Constraints: Freeze Rotation
```

The visual model should be a child so that the physics capsule controls the root rotation.

---

# 2. Surface movement script

This script uses the old Input Manager axes:

```text
Horizontal
Vertical
```

If your Unity 2023 project uses only the new Input System, either set:

```text
Project Settings > Player > Active Input Handling > Both
```

or replace the input reading code with your new Input System actions.

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

[RequireComponent(typeof(Rigidbody), typeof(CapsuleCollider))]
public class SurfaceWalker : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Header("References")]
    [SerializeField] private Transform cameraTransform;
    [SerializeField] private LayerMask walkableLayers;

    [Header("Movement")]
    [SerializeField] private float moveSpeed = 5f;
    [SerializeField] private float acceleration = 35f;
    [SerializeField] private float rotationSpeed = 12f;

    [Header("Surface Attraction")]
    [SerializeField] private float surfaceGravity = 35f;

    [Header("Surface Detection")]
    [SerializeField] private float surfaceSearchDistance = 2.5f;
    [SerializeField] private float currentSurfaceBias = 0.15f;
    [SerializeField] private bool searchAroundCharacter = true;

    private Rigidbody rb;
    private Vector2 moveInput;

    private Vector3 surfaceUp;
    private Vector3 facingDirection;
    private Vector3[] probeDirections;

    private bool hasSurface;

    private void Awake()
    {
        rb = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();

        rb.useGravity = false;
        rb.interpolation = RigidbodyInterpolation.Interpolate;
        rb.collisionDetectionMode = CollisionDetectionMode.ContinuousDynamic;
        rb.constraints = RigidbodyConstraints.FreezeRotation;

        surfaceUp = transform.up;
        facingDirection = transform.forward;

        BuildProbeDirections();
    }

    private void BuildProbeDirections()
    {
        probeDirections = new Vector3[26];

        int index = 0;

        for (int x = -1; x <= 1; x++)
        {
            for (int y = -1; y <= 1; y++)
            {
                for (int z = -1; z <= 1; z++)
                {
                    if (x == 0 && y == 0 && z == 0)
                        continue;

                    probeDirections[index++] = new Vector3(x, y, z).normalized;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    private void Update()
    {
        moveInput = Vector2.ClampMagnitude(
            new Vector2(
                Input.GetAxisRaw("Horizontal"),
                Input.GetAxisRaw("Vertical")
            ),
            1f
        );
    }

    private void FixedUpdate()
    {
        hasSurface = TryFindSurface(out RaycastHit surfaceHit);

        if (hasSurface)
        {
            // Smooth the normal slightly to reduce jitter on faceted meshes.
            surfaceUp = Vector3.Slerp(
                surfaceUp,
                surfaceHit.normal.normalized,
                0.5f
            ).normalized;

            MoveAlongSurface();
        }

        // Custom gravity / surface attraction.
        rb.AddForce(-surfaceUp * surfaceGravity, ForceMode.Acceleration);

        AlignToSurface();
    }

    private void MoveAlongSurface()
    {
        Vector3 forward = GetMovementForward();
        Vector3 right = Vector3.Cross(surfaceUp, forward).normalized;

        Vector3 desiredDirection =
            forward * moveInput.y +
            right * moveInput.x;

        Vector3 desiredVelocity = desiredDirection * moveSpeed;

        // Split current velocity into surface-tangent and surface-normal parts.
        Vector3 tangentVelocity = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(rb.velocity, surfaceUp);
        Vector3 normalVelocity = Vector3.Project(rb.velocity, surfaceUp);

        // Accelerate only along the surface.
        tangentVelocity = Vector3.MoveTowards(
            tangentVelocity,
            desiredVelocity,
            acceleration * Time.fixedDeltaTime
        );

        rb.velocity = tangentVelocity + normalVelocity;

        if (desiredDirection.sqrMagnitude > 0.001f)
        {
            facingDirection = desiredDirection.normalized;
        }
    }

    private Vector3 GetMovementForward()
    {
        Vector3 reference = cameraTransform != null
            ? cameraTransform.forward
            : facingDirection;

        Vector3 forward = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(reference, surfaceUp);

        // If the camera is looking straight down/up relative to the surface,
        // use another fallback.
        if (forward.sqrMagnitude < 0.001f && cameraTransform != null)
        {
            forward = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(cameraTransform.up, surfaceUp);
        }

        if (forward.sqrMagnitude < 0.001f)
        {
            forward = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(facingDirection, surfaceUp);
        }

        if (forward.sqrMagnitude < 0.001f)
        {
            forward = Vector3.Cross(surfaceUp, Vector3.right);
        }

        if (forward.sqrMagnitude < 0.001f)
        {
            forward = Vector3.Cross(surfaceUp, Vector3.forward);
        }

        return forward.normalized;
    }

    private void AlignToSurface()
    {
        Vector3 forward = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(facingDirection, surfaceUp);

        if (forward.sqrMagnitude < 0.001f)
        {
            forward = GetMovementForward();
        }

        facingDirection = forward.normalized;

        Quaternion targetRotation = Quaternion.LookRotation(
            facingDirection,
            surfaceUp
        );

        float blend = 1f - Mathf.Exp(-rotationSpeed * Time.fixedDeltaTime);

        rb.MoveRotation(
            Quaternion.Slerp(
                rb.rotation,
                targetRotation,
                blend
            )
        );
    }

    private bool TryFindSurface(out RaycastHit bestHit)
    {
        bestHit = default;

        Vector3 origin = rb.worldCenterOfMass;

        float bestScore = float.PositiveInfinity;
        bool found = false;

        // Prefer the current "down" direction slightly.
        // This helps avoid snapping too eagerly to nearby walls.
        CheckRay(
            origin,
            -surfaceUp,
            currentSurfaceBias,
            ref bestHit,
            ref bestScore,
            ref found
        );

        // Extra probes help detect adjacent faces around cube edges
        // and other sharp transitions.
        if (searchAroundCharacter)
        {
            foreach (Vector3 direction in probeDirections)
            {
                CheckRay(
                    origin,
                    direction,
                    0f,
                    ref bestHit,
                    ref bestScore,
                    ref found
                );
            }
        }

        return found;
    }

    private void CheckRay(
        Vector3 origin,
        Vector3 direction,
        float preferenceBias,
        ref RaycastHit bestHit,
        ref float bestScore,
        ref bool found)
    {
        if (direction.sqrMagnitude < 0.001f)
            return;

        if (!Physics.Raycast(
                origin,
                direction,
                out RaycastHit hit,
                surfaceSearchDistance,
                walkableLayers,
                QueryTriggerInteraction.Ignore))
        {
            return;
        }

        float score = hit.distance - preferenceBias;

        if (score < bestScore)
        {
            bestScore = score;
            bestHit = hit;
            found = true;
        }
    }
}
```

---

# 3. Inspector setup

On the player script:

```text
