## Notes

Your example packet:

```zig
var eventCodesValues = [_][2]i16{
    .{0, 32767},
    .{1, 0},
    .{2, -32768},
    .{3, 0},
    // ...
};
```

maps directly to this format:

```text
index: int16 little-endian
value: int16 little-endian
```

So the first pair, `{0, 32767}`, becomes:

```text
00 00 FF 7F
```

The second pair, `{1, 0}`, becomes:

```text
01 00 00 00
```

The third pair, `{2, -32768}`, becomes:

```text
02 00 00 80
```

Also, your original client had a function called `createUDPServer()` that bound to port `31415`. The client should not bind to the server port. It only needs an unbound UDP socket for sending.

