Below is a production-oriented SwiftUI implementation using MVVM plus a protocol-based recording service. It records microphone audio with `AVAudioRecorder`, saves the file persistently, exposes the saved URL, provides a real-time amplitude-based “equalizer” visualization, and has two buttons: start and stop/finish.

This example targets iOS 16+, and it also uses the newer iOS 17 microphone permission API when available.

---

## 1. Add microphone permission

Add this to your `Info.plist`:

```xml
<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
<string>We need access to your microphone to record your voice.</string>
```

In Xcode, this is the key:

```text
Privacy - Microphone Usage Description
```

