After `.groupby("query")`, each item has this shape:

```python
{
    "query": "...",
    "items": [ ... ]
}
```

So an aggregation function can be written as:

```python
def aggregate_result(group, config):
    return {
        "query": group["query"],
        "results": group["items"],
    }
```

Or, if you prefer one-argument functions:

```python
def aggregate_result(group):
    return {
        "query": group["query"],
        "results": group["items"],
    }
```

